{"body":"Conjecture: open:creib.forge.conformance.oracle.recover_json_object fails to tell apart two replies that its documented rule requires it to tell apart. The rule reads: \"The object scored is the last one inside a code fence when any fence holds one, else the last top-level object in the text, because a model places its final answer last and marks it: a reply that quotes its previous answer and then gives a corrected one is scored on the correction.\" First reply: '```json\n{\"a\":1} {\"b\":2}\n```\n{\"c\":3}'. Here the code fence holds two objects, {\"a\":1} and {\"b\":2}; the last one inside the fence is {\"b\":2}, so the rule requires the answer {\"b\":2}. Second reply: '{\"c\":3}'. There is no fence, so the rule requires the last top-level object, {\"c\":3}. The conjecture is that recover_json_object returns {\"c\":3} for both replies, giving the same answer where the rule requires different answers. The observation that would show this conjecture false is recover_json_object returning {\"b\":2} for the first reply and {\"c\":3} for the second, or any pair of distinct answers that match the rule's required objects."}